<title>USA: U.S. banks free reserves $696 mln July 30 two wks.</title>
<headline>U.S. banks free reserves $696 mln July 30 two wks.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. commercial banks had free reserves of $696 million per day in the two weeks ended July 30, versus revised free reserves of $1.062 billion in the previous two-week period, the Federal Reserve said.</p>
<p>Seasonal borrowings were $363 million versus $299 million a day. Extended credits were nil.</p>
<p>(( -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660 ))</p>
